{"status": "snippet_created", "follow_up_topic": "How you teach beginners to recognize when to stop and ask an expert", "insight_summary": "You start with a reversible, low-voltage task and ask the learner to explain how they will make it safe; if they cannot explain the isolation step, you practice it before touching the device. A successful attempt includes testing the result and knowing when to stop and ask an expert.", "source_answer": "I start with a reversible low-voltage task and ask the learner to explain how they will make it safe. If they cannot explain the isolation step, we practice that before touching the device. A successful attempt includes testing the result and knowing when to stop and ask an expert.", "saved_record_id": "5832cc7c-96a6-4872-9b7f-456a064279e9", "database_file": "/var/folders/5k/41v463l12sqd84cvgnpm_4t80000gn/T/replica-output-di_xtjq3/000-interviews.sqlite3", "storage_snapshot": "/var/folders/5k/41v463l12sqd84cvgnpm_4t80000gn/T/replica-output-di_xtjq3/001-431c683f-299c-4c7f-8cf9-de9709abbeac.json", "persisted_record": {"id": "5832cc7c-96a6-4872-9b7f-456a064279e9", "current_topic": "Repair workshop teaching", "active_question": "How do you decide when a beginner should attempt a repair?", "source_answer": "I start with a reversible low-voltage task and ask the learner to explain how they will make it safe. If they cannot explain the isolation step, we practice that before touching the device. A successful attempt includes testing the result and knowing when to stop and ask an expert.", "follow_up_topic": "How you teach beginners to recognize when to stop and ask an expert", "insight_summary": "You start with a reversible, low-voltage task and ask the learner to explain how they will make it safe; if they cannot explain the isolation step, you practice it before touching the device. A successful attempt includes testing the result and knowing when to stop and ask an expert."}}
